WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.899 --> 00:00:02.579
- [Narrator] In the Turkish
region of Cappadocia,

00:00:02.579 --> 00:00:04.670
hidden in the hollowed rocks,

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.837
lie some of the oldest
Christian churches in the world.

00:00:11.285 --> 00:00:13.368
The Goreme Open Air Museum is a cluster of

00:00:13.368 --> 00:00:15.411
monasteries and churches dating all

00:00:15.411 --> 00:00:18.328
the way back to the fourth century.

00:00:19.307 --> 00:00:21.928
2.6 million years ago, a volcanic eruption

00:00:21.928 --> 00:00:23.768
of the nearby Mount Erciyes resulted

00:00:23.768 --> 00:00:27.464
in the formation of
mushroom-shaped fairy chimneys.

00:00:27.464 --> 00:00:29.704
Each church that makes up
the Goreme Open Air Museum

00:00:29.704 --> 00:00:32.839
is housed within a
separate soft rock cave.

00:00:32.839 --> 00:00:35.283
More than 10 churches make up the museum.

00:00:35.283 --> 00:00:38.382
Inside each church are wall
paintings known as Frescos,

00:00:38.382 --> 00:00:41.582
examples of old classics from
the Byzantine Art Period.

00:00:41.582 --> 00:00:43.120
These incredible paintings have managed to

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.582
retain their clarity and
colors throughout the years,

00:00:45.582 --> 00:00:48.403
thanks to frequent restorations.

00:00:48.403 --> 00:00:51.092
In 1984, the Goreme Open Air Museum

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:53.336
became one of the first
two sites in Turkey

00:00:53.336 --> 00:00:56.954
to be designated a UNESCO
World Heritage Site.

00:00:56.954 --> 00:00:59.118
But it's the museum's extensive history

00:00:59.118 --> 00:01:00.910
and unique structures that have made it

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.660
one of Cappadocia's most
visited attractions.

